# QA M5 acceptance: the whole journey in one run of the real game, from the
# title through Salzburg, St. Gilgen, Brunnwinkl, Falkenstein (Hackl) and
# St. Wolfgang (the qa_m4_accept_full_route inputs, frames 0-19743: the
# route map St. Wolfgang -> Wolfgangsee in Wait from 19607), then no input:
# the map starts the Wolfgangsee intro after its wait (19971) and play
# begins at 20121 as Hackl Resi with the run carried over (lives 6, score
# 99650, 3 Oblaten). From there the Wolfgangsee inputs of
# qa_m5_flow_hackl_wolfgangsee_to_strobl (its 6470-11786, a route that
# keeps the Hackl, never hurt): the steamer, swans, Gelsen, the lantern
# pontoon checkpoint, the Traundl chain, the regatta and the Strobl quay.
# Wolfgangsee LevelComplete at 24536 (frame 4415 of the stage, as in the
# source replay) still as Hackl, the tally, the route map Wolfgangsee ->
# Strobl (25052; Wait from 25128) and, re-cut in M6 since Strobl is
# playable (it used to end in the teaser and the title with the run
# reset), no START: the map's wait starts the Strobl intro (25428) and
# play begins at 25578 as Hackl Resi with the run carried over (lives 6,
# score 115800, 30 Oblaten); the replay ends 30 frames into Strobl.
# Six LevelCompletes, six checkpoints, no death, no hurt, all deterministic.
level  = salzburg
seed   = 1
source = handwritten
start  = title
expect = complete frames=1772..1772 deaths=0 no_event=Died no_event=Hurt no_event=GameOver event=AxeHit event=ExtraLife event=CheckpointReached event=Stroke
expect = state=playing stage=strobl power=hackl score=115800 lives=6 oblaten=30
